1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,422
Short-circuit operators, typeof, and instanceof. These are quick-fire points in problem

2
00:00:05,522 --> 00:00:08,913
one, and the questions are designed to catch you on one

3
00:00:09,013 --> 00:00:12,404
or two specific values. Let's learn exactly which ones.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:19,254
Everything starts with truthy and falsy. There are only eight falsy

5
00:00:19,354 --> 00:00:24,109
values: false, zero, negative zero, big int zero, the empty string,

6
00:00:24,209 --> 00:00:29,326
null, undefined, and NaN. Memorize that list. Everything else is truthy,

7
00:00:29,426 --> 00:00:33,891
including the string zero, the string false, a string with just

8
00:00:33,991 --> 00:00:37,152
a space, an empty array, and an empty object.

9
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:41,414
Now the operators. AND returns the first falsy value it sees, or

10
00:00:41,514 --> 00:00:45,761
the last value if they're all truthy. OR returns the first truthy

11
00:00:45,861 --> 00:00:49,975
value, or the last value if none are. And the nullish operator,

12
00:00:50,075 --> 00:00:54,256
double question mark, only moves to the right side when the left

13
00:00:54,356 --> 00:00:58,202
side is null or undefined. The key idea: they return one of

14
00:00:58,302 --> 00:01:00,677
the actual values, not true or false.

15
00:01:00,766 --> 00:01:04,665
Exam trap. The string zero is a non-empty string, so

16
00:01:04,765 --> 00:01:08,586
it's truthy. String zero OR Kate gives string zero.

17
00:01:11,666 --> 00:01:14,158
Try each one yourself before I reveal it.

18
00:01:14,233 --> 00:01:19,941
Mike is truthy, so AND keeps going, and returns the last value, 14.5.

19
00:01:20,033 --> 00:01:24,301
String zero is truthy, so OR stops right there and returns it.

20
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:28,548
false is falsy, so AND stops immediately and returns false.

21
00:01:28,633 --> 00:01:32,589
Zero is falsy, so OR moves on, and returns John.

22
00:01:32,666 --> 00:01:35,398
null is falsy, so AND returns null.

23
00:01:35,466 --> 00:01:38,440
One is truthy, then the empty string is falsy,

24
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:41,246
so AND stops and returns the empty string.

25
00:01:41,333 --> 00:01:45,457
All three are falsy, so OR returns the last one, null.

26
00:01:48,833 --> 00:01:52,021
Now compare nullish with OR, side by side.

27
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:56,320
Zero isn't null or undefined, so nullish keeps the zero.

28
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:59,588
But OR treats zero as falsy, and gives John.

29
00:01:59,666 --> 00:02:02,422
Same with the empty string. Nullish keeps it.

30
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:04,272
OR replaces it with default.

31
00:02:04,366 --> 00:02:07,866
null is exactly what nullish is for, so we get x.

32
00:02:07,966 --> 00:02:11,248
undefined falls through to zero, and zero is

33
00:02:11,348 --> 00:02:13,938
kept, so the answer is zero, not 7.

34
00:02:15,333 --> 00:02:19,510
Exam trap. Nullish only falls through on null or undefined,

35
00:02:19,610 --> 00:02:22,771
so zero and the empty string are kept. Use it

36
00:02:22,871 --> 00:02:25,961
when zero is a valid value, like a quantity.

37
00:02:29,033 --> 00:02:33,033
Optional chaining. Normally, reading a property of null throws a

38
00:02:33,133 --> 00:02:37,453
TypeError. With question-mark-dot, it just stops and gives undefined.

39
00:02:37,533 --> 00:02:40,673
When everything exists, it works like a normal dot.

40
00:02:40,766 --> 00:02:44,578
prof dot phone is undefined, so the chain stops before home.

41
00:02:44,666 --> 00:02:46,672
And it works for method calls too.

42
00:02:46,772 --> 00:02:49,150
greet doesn't exist, so it isn't called.

43
00:02:49,533 --> 00:02:55,985
undefined, 2 0 7 4 2, undefined, and undefined. No errors anywhere.

44
00:02:59,066 --> 00:03:02,758
typeof always returns a string. Here are the ones people miss.

45
00:03:02,833 --> 00:03:05,734
typeof null is object. That's a famous old

46
00:03:05,834 --> 00:03:09,165
bug in JavaScript, and a favorite exam question.

47
00:03:09,233 --> 00:03:12,325
Arrays are objects, so typeof gives object.

48
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,940
Functions get their own answer: function.

49
00:03:15,033 --> 00:03:16,997
A class is really a function too.

50
00:03:17,066 --> 00:03:20,134
NaN means not a number, but its type is number.

51
00:03:20,233 --> 00:03:22,917
undefined gives the string undefined.

52
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,356
And quotes make it a string, even if it looks like a number.

53
00:03:27,733 --> 00:03:31,590
Exam trap. typeof null is object, and typeof NaN is

54
00:03:31,690 --> 00:03:35,625
number. To test for an array, use Array dot isArray.

55
00:03:38,700 --> 00:03:41,689
instanceof asks one question: is this constructor's

56
00:03:41,789 --> 00:03:44,840
prototype somewhere on the object's prototype chain?

57
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:48,433
An array's chain includes Array dot prototype, so true.

58
00:03:48,533 --> 00:03:50,844
And that chain continues to Object dot

59
00:03:50,944 --> 00:03:53,065
prototype, so this is true as well.

60
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:55,613
A string literal is a primitive, not

61
00:03:55,713 --> 00:03:58,265
an object, so instanceof gives false.

62
00:03:58,333 --> 00:04:01,089
But new String makes a wrapper object, so true.

63
00:04:01,166 --> 00:04:04,234
null has no prototype chain at all, so false.

64
00:04:07,633 --> 00:04:10,213
Practice question 1. What is each of these

65
00:04:10,313 --> 00:04:12,765
five values? Pause the video and try it.

66
00:04:21,033 --> 00:04:26,579
a1 is 10, because zero is falsy. a2 is zero, because nullish keeps

67
00:04:26,679 --> 00:04:32,482
zero. a3 is yes, because the string false is truthy. a4 is undefined,

68
00:04:32,582 --> 00:04:38,128
because neither is truthy, so OR returns the last one. And a5: qty

69
00:04:38,228 --> 00:04:42,149
AND x stops at zero, and typeof zero is number.

70
00:04:46,233 --> 00:04:50,453
Practice question 2. What does this print? Pause the video and try it.

71
00:04:58,733 --> 00:05:02,772
A single space, NaN, Ann, and an empty array. The space

72
00:05:02,872 --> 00:05:06,911
is a non-empty string, so it's truthy. NaN is falsy, so

73
00:05:07,011 --> 00:05:10,824
AND returns it. Ann is truthy. And an empty array is

74
00:05:10,924 --> 00:05:14,737
truthy, so OR returns the array, not the word empty.

75
00:05:18,833 --> 00:05:22,707
Recap. AND returns the first falsy value, or the last one.

76
00:05:22,807 --> 00:05:26,750
OR returns the first truthy value, or the last one. Nullish

77
00:05:26,850 --> 00:05:31,821
only falls through on null or undefined. Optional chaining gives undefined

78
00:05:31,921 --> 00:05:36,069
instead of an error. Know the eight falsy values, and remember

79
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:40,249
that string zero and empty arrays are truthy. And typeof null

80
00:05:40,349 --> 00:05:42,853
is object, while typeof NaN is number.

